    "tips": {
      "title": "Quick Safety Tips",
      "tip1": "Never share your Nafath or Absher OTP codes with anyone, even if they claim to be from a government agency.",
      "tip2": "Check the sender's email address carefully. Official emails from Saudi banks never ask for your password.",
      "tip3": "If you receive a call claiming to be from a ministry, hang up and call the official number directly.",
      "tip4": "Legitimate organizations like SAMA and banks will never ask for your full card number via SMS.",
      "tip5": "Be cautious of messages claiming you won a prize from STC, Mobily, or Zain. Verify through official apps.",
      "tip6": "Enable two-factor authentication on all your accounts, especially Absher and banking apps."
